# KRAN Design System Portal

## Landing vs footer vs header

- **`/home` landing cards:** Module 1 and Module 2 only — `PORTAL_LANDING_MODULES` in `portalModules.js` (ids `module-1`, `module-2`).
- **Footer:** Component Workbench and Design Guidelines (`PORTAL_FOOTER_MODULES` / `AppFooter.jsx`).
- **Header Setup icon:** Administration (setup + asset) — not a landing module card.

## Active domain folders (`src/domain/`)

`administration` (setup + asset), `auth`, `component-workbench`, `dashboard` (inbox tabs), `design-guidelines`, `module-1`, `module-2` (nested `hrms/`, `tasks/` under module-2).

Canonical URL prefixes: `/module-1`, `/module-2`. Legacy `/sample-module/*` and `/workforce/*` redirect via `canonicalizeModulePathname`.

Do not reintroduce duplicate top-level domains (`setup`, `asset`, `hrms`, `task-management`, `component-explorer`, `ui-component-library`).

## Page registry

- Merge domain route maps in `src/app/routes/loadDomainPages.js` (`DASHBOARD_PAGE_REGISTRY`).
- Keys: `'primaryId:secondaryId'` → `lazyPage(() => import(...))`.
- Register every navigable tab; use `getModuleRoute(primaryId, secondaryId)` — no `/dashboard` prefix, no `:accountId` in paths.

## Setup return navigation

Before entering Setup from another module, persist return route via `setupReturnNav.js`. Header Home from Setup restores that route; otherwise `/home`.

## Docs

Long-form architecture and onboarding: repository `docs/` (not duplicated in rules).
